    what: "#448 (parity audit T17): a Tool Forge shuriken -- four wood knife blades -- after one throw. The ProjectileCore layer deliberately introduces NO new serialized format: ammo is durability (`minecraft:damage` 10 = one throw of the ten-durability ratio, 4 of 5 ammo left), so this pins that a shuriken is an ordinary tool stack -- a four-entry `tool_materials` with no handle or binding, the head+extra dual-read stats (durability 35 + 15, attack 2 + 1), and the trait list its blades collected from both scopes, deduplicated to wood's one. ShurikenGameTests#throwCostsOneAmmoAndSpawnsTheProjectile assembles this exact shuriken at a real Tool Forge and asserts these numbers."
